\title{NationalModelUng2009: National Stand-Volume Models for Canadian Tree Species (Ung et al. 2009)}
\description{
Implements the two national growth-and-yield models of Ung, Bernier, Guo and Lambert (2009) \doi{10.5558/tfc85057-1}. Given stand age, annual degree-days above 0 C and mean annual precipitation, 'Nat1' predicts dominant height, basal area and gross merchantable volume, and 'Nat2' predicts volume directly, for 25 Canadian commercial tree species. The package validates inputs, warns when a prediction falls outside the data the models were fitted to or is very sensitive to the climate inputs, and can look up climate values with the 'climr' package.
}
\details{
Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ung_yield_table]{ung_yield_table()}} makes tables of volume by age (yield curves), for
example for the Carbon Budget Model, and plots them.
\item \link{ung_models} explains the models, their climate inputs and their limits.
\item \code{\link[=ung_check]{ung_check()}} lists the cautions that apply to a set of predictions.
\item \code{\link[=ung_climate]{ung_climate()}} looks up degree-days and precipitation with climr or
ClimateNA.
\item \code{\link[=ung_species]{ung_species()}} lists the 25 supported species.
}
